{
  "description": "Syntax colours of code blocks (Q-D13, step 8, research/14 §6.17). The oracle the runtime syntax checks (tests/runtime/lib/syntax.mjs) compare Obsidian's computed colours with: for every text range of the code blocks of `note`, the colour variable this theme should give it, found from these rules the way the cascade finds it (on the innermost element, the matching rule with the most classes wins, the later one on a tie; with no matching rule, the parent element; then Obsidian's own rules in `obsidian`; then `default`). `on` = classes of the element, `in` = classes of one ancestor element, `not` = classes the element must not have, `lang` = the block's fence names; `langAliases` names the language a fence name belongs to, for grouping (the class check, syn.<view>.classes). `var` is a --ink-syntax-<var>-color, `code` an Obsidian --code-<code> variable resolved through `codeVars` (src/common/mapping/syntax.css). The Inkdrop side is `inkdrop` (generated by tests/visual/inkdrop-tokens.mjs from Inkdrop 6.1.5's own parsers and token table).",
